{
  "date": "2026-10-21T13:40:39.434Z",
  "commit": "b20ce53",
  "what": "How long the walk back through a line's history takes, and what it sends, on the cases of the gold set, with no model. Each case is collected once, then walked with the limits the app uses and again with the time limit cut to 300 ms, to see the requests in flight cancelled on a real network. A hosted repository is walked through the GitHub API, a seeded one through git. The answer's time is the one kept for the same case in the current run, through OpenRouter pinned to Groq. The app runs the walk beside the writer and the audit and sends the answer before it waits for the walk, so a walk longer than the answer only brings the earlier history after it.",
